**Migration `0042_add_settlement_currency`** is the schema change that ran as the second step of the `v412` release job, at 14:05. In one transaction it:

```sql
ALTER TABLE ledger_entries ADD COLUMN settlement_currency char(3);
UPDATE ledger_entries SET settlement_currency = 'USD';
ALTER TABLE ledger_entries ALTER COLUMN settlement_currency SET NOT NULL;
```

The column is `NOT NULL` with no default, so every insert has to supply it. `v411` doesn't write that column. After the migration ran, setting the config back to `legacy` (14:21) or rolling back to `v411` (14:33) still left inserts failing, this time on a not-null violation. The fix was to roll forward to `v412`, which writes `settlement_currency` in either mode.

